+# P1517 local terminal receiver candidate
+
+This file preserves the P1517 historical result and limitations below.
+The successor's separate local verification is recorded in
+[REVALIDATION-C1177.md](REVALIDATION-C1177.md); it does not reset P1517's FIRST,
+RED, exhausted budget or ENV-PARTIAL result.
+
+Parent: unadopted PR1508 HEAD `7591848bd7f4bf8967dffd4be8d360e1901a3f06`.
+Operational/canonical authority: adopted main `4c388693b95f371783e666f5c77e0aec5d17d215`, CURRENT_SPEC → Draft17.38.
+
+This private C17 consumer factors the second original H terminal cleanup into
+its genuine §18.1a callee, then cleans the first original in the caller before
+the second named Copy into the same original T. The exact owner call is borrowed
+from the authenticated H2 arm; all existing root/incarnation/R/Domain, actual/
+formal, full-range, source/world and affine checks remain mandatory. No checker,
+public issuer, source law, API or ABI changes are made.
+
+Coverage is bounded to the existing direct two-H mixed-unit/current-Copy lane:
+startup named Copy; two normal allocation matches; one payload read under the
+second original Domain; one step-count4 terminal receiver of that original;
+caller first-H cleanup; same-original named Copy. No producer/LiveTail or link
+write is introduced. Optional receiver reads (step-count5), general ownership,
+arbitrary additional calls/control flow, and receiver field-index1 native
+coverage are not claimed. Existing inline direct and linked producer paths keep
+their separate gates.
+
+P-zero/P-nonzero and the six original negatives/public_owned.c preserve P1515
+FIRST bytes. N-foreign-pointer adds the wrong p0 actual. H1 leak remains a
+precision refusal; stale read is rejected at consumed Domain use, before ref
+issuance. The native observer checks true allocation identities, distinct
+Domains, closed read scopes, second-original free inside receiver, first free
+outside, H0/H1 no second T write, and real zero-success T write/old/sibling.
+It observes addresses before real free and clears saved pointers. It creates no
+program state or ownership.
+
+Local evidence: GCC O0/O2 × two sources × H0/H1/H2 = 12 PASS; six old inline
+worlds and one linked producer native regression PASS; public MACHINE/owner/
+Copy validators PASS; 35 artifact mutations and seven source negatives reject;
+six host OOM sites plus named-output rollback/retry PASS. Eighteen CTests were
+registered; one registered public-owned CTest was executed, with the remaining
+relevant probes/native operations exercised directly under a counted ledger.
+No full CTest/CI pass is claimed.
+
+C1163 accepts ENV-PARTIAL for this local-only mission. Mandatory pinned Clang
+validation is NOT_RUN: exact project-lock Debian Clang23
+package URL returned HTTP404 on three requests and there is no installed Clang.
+Precisely, the lock top-level LLVM version is23.1.3, while its Debian legacy
+clang-23 artifact URL/version is23.1.2. That Debian URL was the failed request;
+neither version was installed or validated here.
+ASan/UBSan/format tool are NOT_RUN. Aggregate local charges80/80, selected guest19/36,
+selected host OOM sites6/16, fault/retry cases16/48. Initial private compile and
+observer compile REDs are preserved; history/passive-v1.h.data is the original
+malformed observer, active tests use separately frozen passive-v2.h.
+
+This is LOCAL ONLY / DRAFT NOT_RELEASED. It is not full-vertical PASS or an
+adopted compiler. Publication requires C's PR1508 disposition, actual adopted
+base/tree integration release, and genuine fixed-head Clang/ASan/UBSan plus
+selected native/format/independent safety validation under the subsequent C
+release. Additional local work needs a new budget; local80/80 is immutable. No remote Production push, PR or CI
+was performed.
+
+VALUE-ALIGNMENT-RISK: author+ordinary-safe caller UB audit/re-audit dependency
+reduction versus well-factored C remains UNMEASURED; sound Rust owned/Drop or
+safe facade remains a fair alternative. Product GO624 PAUSED / H1#268 HOLD.
