+## Exact supported increment
+
+The existing direct two-H mixed H/T lane admits one genuine four-step
+terminal receiver of the second original H after its scoped payload read.
+The callee ends that original lifetime, recovers its full original Storage,
+finalizes its original Domain and deallocates its original Allocation once.
+The caller then ends the first original H, and the named Copy updates the
+same original T field. H0/H1 have no phantom receiver or second T write;
+payload0 in H2 is genuine success. Actual/formal/body/result, original
+root/incarnation/R/Domain, whole-root source ownership, closed loan scopes,
+current/old Copy and affine consumption remain mandatory.
+
+No checker, public issuer, source law, API/ABI, LLVM lowering, producer or
+LiveTail capability is added. Optional five-step receiver-internal reads,
+receiver field-index1, arbitrary forwarding/owner/CFG compositions and
+general safe APIs remain outside this implementation. Existing inline direct
+and linked producer paths retain their original independent guards.
